</p>

<p>
  The ablation result has a striking ordering: removing insight propagation hurts <em>more</em> than removing
  the tree itself. A tree without propagated lessons can organize experiments syntactically but provides no
  semantic memory. The tree and insight propagation together are what makes each experiment informative for all future ones.
</p>

<div class="callout amber">
